# Separation of concerns (frontend)

Every page/component file has **one job: compose UI and wire props**. Do not mix raw API calls into large page files for new work.

## Layout

| Concern | Location | Contains |
|---------|----------|----------|
| UI | `src/pages/`, `src/components/` | JSX, local UI state, layout |
| API | `src/api/` | Axios calls — **no React** |
| Hooks | `src/hooks/` / feature hooks | react-query orchestration |
| Utils | `src/utils/` | Pure helpers |
| UI kit | `src/components/ui/` | Redesign primitives |

## Do

- Pages import hooks + presentational components; hooks/pages call `src/api/`
- Define every backend path in `src/api/` — never hardcode URLs in components
- Keep files ≤ 350 lines; split by concern when growing

## Don't

- Call `axios` / hardcode routes inside a page for new work
- Colocate API helpers at the bottom of a page “for convenience”
- Bypass `paystack-api.ts` for payment starts/declares
